#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:934
msgid ""
"Now setuptools declares its own dependencies in the ``core`` extra. "
"Dependencies are still vendored for bootstrapping purposes, but setuptools "
"will prefer installed dependencies if present. The ``core`` extra is used "
"for informational purposes and should *not* be declared in package metadata "
"(e.g. ``build-requires``). Downstream packagers can de-vendor by simply "
"removing the ``setuptools/_vendor`` directory. Since Setuptools now prefers "
"installed dependencies, those installing to an environment with old, "
"incompatible dependencies will not work. In that case, either uninstall the "
"incompatible dependencies or upgrade them to satisfy those declared in "
"``core``. (`#2825 <https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/2825>`_)"
msgstr ""

