"that all of a namespace package's ``__init__.py`` files must include a "
"``declare_namespace()`` call in order to ensure that they will be handled "
"properly at runtime. In 2.x it was possible to get away without including "
"the declaration, but only at the cost of forcing namespace packages to be "
"imported early, which 3.0 no longer does."
